  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 905.02 Collection, Storage, and Transfer Requirements",
  "priorExpiration": "1997-07-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 905.02 Collection, Storage, and Transfer Requirements.\n\n(a) Tires shall be collected, stored, and transferred in accordance with Env-Sw 400 and this section.\n\n(b) Outdoor storage of tires shall be in:\n\n(1) Covered trailers;\n\n(2) Transfer containers; or\n\n(3) In stockpiles as follows:\n\na. The diameter of the piles shall not exceed 25 feet;\n\nb. The height of the piles shall not exceed 15 feet;\n\nc. Fire lanes no less than 25 feet in width shall be maintained around each pile;\n\nd. Each pile shall have a berm with a minimum height of 12 inches constructed around its perimeter capable of containing any pyrolitic oils or other liquids generated by fire; and\n\ne. The stockpiling facility shall have equipment, cover material, and other supplies, including water, sufficient to control a fire until the nearest fire company capable of extinguishing the fire arrives.\n\n(c) Indoor storage shall conform to the applicable requirements of Saf-C 6000.\n\nSource. #5172, eff 7-1-91, EXPIRED: 7-1-97\n\nNew. #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 900); ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 2605.02); ss by #10598, eff 7-1-14; ss by #14067, eff 9-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw900.html"
